"Trades bishop for knight."]},{"ply":33,"name":"17.Rhe1","cls":"miss","color":"w","headline":"17.Rhe1 misses the chance 16…Re8 gave: 17.Bf2 would have punished it. White's winning chances go from 62% to 48%.","points":["Black answers 17…Bd3: the bishop on d3 can be taken by the c2 pawn or the queen on d2.","Better was 17.Bf2 (+1.35): shores up the knight on d4, which was under as much attack as it had defence (1 against 1)."],"better":"17.Bf2 shores up the knight on d4. Engine line: 17…d5 18.b3 Ba6 19.exd5 Nxd5 20.Nf5 (+1.35)."},{"ply":87,"name":"44.Be3","cls":"blunder","color":"w","headline":"44.Be3 is a blunder: White's winning chances go from 50% to 15%.","points":["Black answers 44…Rb2+, which gives check, so the reply is forced.","Better was 44.Rxg4 (−0.03), which takes the pawn on g4."],"better":"44.Rxg4 wins a pawn. After 44…h2 45.Rf4+ Ke8 46.Rf1 Rb2+ 47.Kd3, White comes out a pawn up (−0.03)."},{"ply":88,"name":"44…h2","cls":"miss","color":"b","headline":"44…h2 misses the chance 44.Be3 gave: 44…Rb2+ would have punished it. Black's winning chances go from 85% to 52%.","points":["White answers 45.Bf4, which attacks the h2 pawn, which is undefended.","The pawn on h2 can be taken by the rook on h4.","After Bf4, White wins 1 point of material within 6 moves.","Better was 44…Rb2+ (−4.78), which gives check, so the reply is forced."],"better":"44…Rb2+ gives check. Engine line: 45.Kc1 Rg2 46.Bf4 Kg6 47.Bd6 Kf5 (−4.78)."},{"ply":89,"name":"45.Bf4","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"45.Bf4! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Attacks the h2 pawn, which is undefended.","The next best move, 45.Rh7+, would drop White's winning chances from 48% to 9% (−6.29).","45.Bf4 wins a pawn, picking it up with 46.Rxh3.","Sets up a sequence and wins a pawn once the captures settle, picking it up with 46.Rxh3.","Black answers 45…Rh3.","After 45…Rh3 46.Rxh3 gxh3 47.Bxh2 b3 48.Kc1, the rooks are traded and White comes out a pawn up (−0.06)."]},{"ply":91,"name":"46.Bxg3","cls":"brilliant","color":"w","headline":"46.Bxg3!! A real sacrifice: White gives up material and the engine still rates it best.","points":["Puts the bishop on g3 where it can be taken.","Black can take, but after 46…Rxg3 47.Rxh2 Ke6 48.Rh5 the engine rates it 0.00.","Takes the pawn on g3.","Leaves Black with an isolated pawn on h2: a long-term weakness.","46.Bxg3 leaves Black with an isolated pawn on h2 and opens the line of the rook on h4 to the b4 pawn.","Moving away uncovers the rook on h4, which now hits the b4 pawn."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"46.Bxg3!! gives up the bishop on g3 to stay in the game: after it White holds the balance (0.00); anything else leaves White losing (−4.29)."},{"title":"What White gives up","text":"46.Bxg3 puts the bishop on g3 where it can be taken by the rook on b3. That's a bishop on offer."},{"title":"If Black takes the bishop","text":"46…Rxg3 is met by 47.Rxh2, taking the h2 pawn. Then 48.Rh5 attacks the b5 pawn, which is undefended, and 49.Rxb5 takes the b5 pawn. Material is level and White holds the balance (0.00). This is Black's best try."},{"title":"Without the sacrifice","text":"The best move without the sacrifice, 46.Kc2, is clearly weaker (−4.29 against 0.00). Black answers 46…Rc3+. That would leave White losing."}]},{"ply":156,"name":"78…Kc3","cls":"blunder","color":"b","headline":"78…Kc3 is a blunder: Black's winning chances go from 50% to 10%.","points":["White answers 79.Rb3+, which skewers the king: when it moves, the rook on h3 behind it falls.","After Rb3+, White wins 5 points of material within 4 moves.","Better was 78…Kc4 (0.00): the king steps out of check to c4."],"better":"78…Kc4 prepares …Kd3 and …Rh8 and steps the king out of check to c4. Engine line: 79.Rc1+ Kd3 80.Kb2 Rh8 81.Rd1+ Kc4 (0.00)."},{"ply":157,"name":"79.Rb3+","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"79.Rb3+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Skewers the king: when it moves, the rook on h3 behind it falls.","Gives check, so the reply is forced.","The next best move, 79.Rc1+, would drop White's winning chances from 90% to 50% (0.00).","79.Rb3+ wins a rook, picking it up with 80.Rxh3.","Sets up a sequence and wins a rook once the captures settle, picking it up with 80.Rxh3.","Black answers 79…Kc4, uncovering an attack on the rook on b3."]}],"opening":{"name":"Scotch Game: Potter Variation","eco":"C45","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 7…Nf6: 14 moves in all, 7 by White and 7 by Black.","Theory runs out after 7…Nf6: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}